From: mscharged-port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Keep device validation and robustness independent of debug layers
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: native graphics device correctness policy.

The backend validation preference controls optional API debug layers. It must
not also disable Dawn command validation or robust buffer/shader accesses in
Release. Preserve all device features, descriptors, source commands and the
existing default with debug layers enabled.

diff --git a/lib/webgpu/gpu.cpp b/lib/webgpu/gpu.cpp
--- a/lib/webgpu/gpu.cpp
+++ b/lib/webgpu/gpu.cpp
@@ -985,12 +985,8 @@
         "enable_immediate_error_handling",
         "gl_allow_context_on_multi_threads",
     };
-#ifdef NDEBUG
-    if (!g_config.enableBackendValidation) {
-      enableToggles.push_back("skip_validation");
-      enableToggles.push_back("disable_robustness");
-    }
-#endif
+    // Backend debug layers are independent of Dawn command validation and
+    // robust buffer/shader access, which remain enabled in every build.
     constexpr std::array disableToggles{
         "timestamp_quantization",
         // Adreno strikes again!
